                {
                  "id": "h-protect-system",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "How to Protect Your Semi Truck Electrical System",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "protect-system"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-protect-system-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Preventive care prevents breakdowns and extends the life of your new battery. Here's how to keep your electrical system healthy and reduce long-term repair costs.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "checks-protect-system-2",
                  "type": "check-list",
                  "props": {
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Perform routine battery testing"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Limit excessive idling"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Inspect cables and connections regularly"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Choose the best semi truck batteries for your equipment"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-protect-system-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Routine voltage checks can reveal early performance dips before they turn into roadside problems, and our service centers provide full electrical diagnostics to ensure your system is operating correctly. Idling drains your battery faster than many drivers realize, and loose or corroded cables can mimic battery failure symptoms. Not all batteries are designed for the same loads, climates, or starting demands; Sun State International can help you select the best semi truck batteries based on your truck's requirements, driving patterns, and electrical load.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "fig-2",
                  "type": "image",
                  "props": {
                    "width": "full",
                    "image": {
                      "src": "/img/blog/signs-its-time-to-replace-your-semi-truck-battery/2.jpg",
                      "width": 1280,
                      "height": 853,
                      "alt": "Exterior of Sun State International service center with truck bays ready for maintenance"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
